> 
> 
> Did anybody else observe this effect?  Could it be some compile time option?


You might look in /var/log/dmesg.  See if it complains about a "bogus" 
clock cycle frequency.

Also look in /proc/cpuinfo to see if the "cycle freqency [Hz]" is correct.

You might need to pass the the kernel the correct frequency as an argument:

boot vmlinuz -flags root=/dev/sda2 cycle=xxxxxxxxx

(xxxxxxxxx=correct frequency of your CPU)

We had this problem with 2.4.3-12 a kernel, although it was only about 
4% off.

