Willix <william.keyser@compaq.com> wrote:
> Hello all,
> I've just received an 'old' AlphaStation 500 and I'd like to install RedHat
> Linux7.1 on it. I've done some Linux installation on PC's and Laptops but I
> am new to Alpha and all the stuff of SRM, ARC, MILO.
> -How do I know which firmware my system has?
> -Is MILO the equivalent of LILO (ie a OS loader)?
> -On most modern PCs, one can type F2 or F6 at boot time to enter the BIOS
> setup page and decide the order in which the BIOS has to look for a OS
> (floppy, Hard drive, CD). Can one do the same on an Alpha and if so, which
> key(s) do you hit at boot time?
> -Could someone point me to a concise tutorial on SRM, ARC and so on.

> Many thanks
> w.

Just switch your maschine on and you will see, whitch console you have
currently. Most maschines have both (not at the same time ;-) ). If you are
in Arc-Console, you have a kind of menu and to boot via MILO. If you are in
SRM you'll see a >>>-prompt. The way to boot via SRM and aboot is easer
IMHO. There yuo can see, what hardware you have (type >>>sh dev).

If you like to boot, you have to figure out, how the name of your CD-drive
is. F.e. to boot from diskette type >>>boot dva0 -fl 0 or to boot from CD
type >>>boot dka400 -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl root=/dev/scd0 . dka400 is a
CD-drive whith ID 4 (see >>>sh dev )!

Good luck!

Bye

Frank Sackewitz

