The screen switching to red background is perfectly normal (you still
have white text, don't you?). If the machine freezes there it means
the kernel has hung on something just after it swithch the screen
colors. Check if there are any other kernels on the disk which might
work better. If you at the SRM prompt type 'boot dka4 -flags "i"'
(replace dka4 with name of your cdrom, my cdrom is scsi id 4), you
will get an aboot prompt. There type 'l' to list any preconfigured
kernels or 'd /boot' to list all files in directory /boot on the cd.

