Originally the machine had ARC console firmware version 3.5-13 (1993), 
with that version the card was identified on booting as 
"Video: 8 plane frame buffer ..... TGA 8 Plane". 
In order to support the new card (Matrox Millennium G200 SD), 
I had to upgrade the ARC firmware; I installed version 4.58. 
Now the same card was identified as 
"Video: 8 plane frame buffer ..... ZLXp-E1".

My conclusion is that the string returned for the card depends 
on the firmware version. Others might tell whether this 
output also gets to the X server.

Before the firmware upgrade, I used SuSE AXP 7.0 with the TGA 
X driver ("xtga-3.3.6-85"), it worked fine. 
(The original installation had been SuSE 6.1, then upgraded.) 
After the firmware upgrade, I immediately changed the card, 
so I can not tell whether it still worked.

By now, the card is changed, so I can not give you the "lspci" 
output for it. 
However, on my machine the address "00:0b.0" is the Ethernet 
controller (Digital 21040 Tulip), 
my (new) graphic card is at "00:0d.0" (same slot as old card). 
The complete output is  
00:0b:0 VGA compatible controller: Matrox Graphics, Inc. MGA G200 ... 
  Subsystem: ...
  Memory at 0000000005000000 (32-bit, prefetchable) 
  Memory at 0000000006000000 (32-bit, non-prefetchable) 
  Memory at 0000000006800000 (32-bit, non-prefetchable) 
  Expansion ROM at 00000000000c0000 
  Capabilities: [dc] Power Management version 1
I do not know whether the different address and IRQ are significant.

