On CD #1 there is a directory called "disks" which contains the images
for the installation disks, for my equipment that would be "noname"
for the milo disk and "install" for the installation disk.
Question #1  What hides behind "install_" ?

The readme (written for 6.1. Shame on Suse !) says to start milo via
ARC and at the milo-prompt to boot the system by entering
"boot fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0".
If the milo-disk is still in the drive, I get the message that
"vmlinux.gz" is not on the disk and the kernel could not be booted.
Well, I have another disk...
If the installation disk is in the drive, I get the message that the
filesystem is unknown and the kernel could not be booted.
I'm out of disks now...

Suses support database states that the command for booting should read
